.TH GROUPS "1" "2026-07-28" "BNU 9.11" "BNU Commands"
.SH NAME
groups \- print the groups a user is in
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B groups
[\fI\,OPTION\/\fR]... [\fI\,USERNAME\/\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.\" This page is derived from GNU Coreutils documentation.
This page documents BNU, an independent Bun implementation compatible with
GNU Coreutils 9.11.
.PP
Print group memberships for each USERNAME or, if no USERNAME is specified, for
the current process (which may differ if the groups database has changed).
